"""Normalized probability, support on the energy surface and actual averages."""
from ch05_data import add,copied,proposition,D,NS
add('MicroMeasure','5.3.3',194,[52],r'''Let $d\mu_E=Z_E^{-1}\|\nabla H\|^{-1}d\sigma$. We refer to this as the microcanonical probability density and write, for an “appropriate” set $A$, $\operatorname{Pr}(A)=\mu_E(A)=\int_A d\mu_E$. The only requirement for this to make sense is that the set $A$ be a measurable subset of the $H=E$ energy surface, i.e. that it be possible to compute its surface area.''',copied(D,'microMeasure'),kind='definition',extra=['[EXTRA]总raw质量正且有限是使用概率意义的必要资格；定义用实际ENNReal标量归一化，不把无穷总质量逆值0解释成概率测度。'])
add('MicroProbability','5.3.3',195,[53],r'''We have the standard properties of a probability function: $0\leq\operatorname{Pr}(A)\leq1$ for all measurable sets $A$; $\operatorname{Pr}(\Sigma_E)=1$.''',f'''theorem microProbability : ∀ n (H : {NS}E n → ℝ) c,
  ContDiff ℝ 1 H → 0 < ({NS}microRaw H c) univ → ({NS}microRaw H c) univ < (⊤ : ENNReal) →
  ({NS}microMeasure H c) univ=1 ∧
    ({NS}microMeasure H c) ({NS}energySurface H c)=1 ∧
    ∀ A : Set ({NS}E n),0 ≤ ({NS}microMeasure H c) A ∧ ({NS}microMeasure H c) A ≤ 1 := by
  sorry''',extra=['[EXTRA]原H光滑背景及正有限总质量明示；ΣE总概率1也保留，不仅证明ambient univ质量1。'],missing='待实际withDensity/restrict及ENNReal逆标量归一化短桥，不需要coarea理论。')
add('LowerDimensionNull','5.3.3',195,[54],r'''We also note that lower order objects such as a point or a curve in $\mathbb R^2$, or a surface in $\mathbb R^3$, have zero measure with respect to Lebesgue measure for the ambient space. Similarly, for a Hamiltonian system with $N_d$ degrees of freedom, the energy surface is of dimension $2N_d-1$ and the probability measure of sets of lower dimension than this will vanish.''',proposition('lowerDimensionNull_statement'),extra=['[EXTRA]低维光滑参数化的紧像、正则C¹能量面，维数严格小于能量面；未将任意“拓扑低维集合”自动视为零测。'],missing='缺Hausdorff维数/光滑图像到真实曲面加权测度零集的接口；不建设大型几何理论。')
add('MicroAverage','5.3.3',195,[55],r'''As we mentioned in motivating the microcanonical distribution, we could alternatively view microcanonical averages as integrals with respect to the singular measure on the ambient space $D$ defined by $\mu_Ed\omega'=Z_E^{-1}\delta[H-E]d\omega$. Regardless of which formulation is adopted, we may use the probability measure to compute expectations (averages) of (suitable) functions defined on the phase space. We write such an expectation as
\[\operatorname{Av}_{H=E}(g)=\int_{\Sigma_E}g(z)d\mu_E=\int_Dg(z)\mu_Ed\omega'.\]
As shorthand, where the underlying space and probability density are assumed, one may write such an average more simply as $\operatorname{Av}_{H=E}(g)=\langle g\rangle$.''',copied(D,'microAverage'),kind='definition',context=['实际归一化奇异测度上的积分；δ[H−E]是分布记号，面积/δ两描述的识别是未证明的coarea义务，不称普通Lebesgue密度。'])
